<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Chapter 2</a> &gt; Level 13</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 13 Walkthrough: Grocery Store</h1>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt frame by frame from a recorded playthrough of the current build — 16 minutes 32 seconds of footage, extracted at one frame per second, with slower passes at four and eight frames per second over every panel that carries a number, read at up to 6× zoom. Two numbers are published here. The exit code <b>65219</b> was read digit by digit at 6× zoom, and a second, independent recording of the same level also ends on it. The drinks-fridge code <b>02725</b> was read twice at 6× zoom from the frame where the dials settle, with the frames either side showing them stepping to it, but it comes from a single recording. Two things in this room could not be read twice — the order the eight vent buttons want, and the path the locker board accepts — so this page describes those two puzzles and sends you to the in-game clue instead of printing a sequence we might have wrong.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={2} current={13} variant="jump" label="Chapter 2 · No Honor Among Thieves" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>The Grocery Store runs on two five-digit numbers and four barcodes: <b>02725</b> on the dials under the drinks fridge, and <b>65219</b> on the plate under the self-checkout counter at the very end. Finish worth <b>+50 coins</b>.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Take the <b>wallet</b> from the blue basket by the self-scan till, then <b>Dismantle</b> it → <b>coin</b> + <b>Code</b> card (<b>58431267</b>).</li>
        <li>Collect the <b>orange</b>, the <b>hammer</b> and the <b>marker</b> from the produce bins, and the <b>green shovel</b> from the blue lockers.</li>
        <li>Use the <b>coin</b> on the four screws of the <b>vent cover</b> → eight-button panel. Press the buttons in the order on the Code card (they are not the modules above them).</li>
        <li>Clear the <b>number board</b> that opens on the locker screen → <b>hand barcode reader</b>.</li>
        <li>Tap the rows of cans in the drinks fridge to reveal five digits, then set the dials under it to <b>02725</b> → <b>key</b>.</li>
        <li>Key opens the second drinks fridge → <b>bottle</b>. Read the <b>four barcodes</b>: tins by the bread, a yellow soda can, the ice cream in the chest freezer, and the juicer's receipt.</li>
        <li><b>Hammer</b> the cracked freezer pane and <b>dig the flower pot</b> → two <b>gear parts</b> → combine → <b>gear</b> for the juicer.</li>
        <li>Put the reader on the till by the baskets, clear the <b>dot grid</b>, then dial <b>65219</b> into the five-slot plate under the counter. Press the <b>red button</b> underneath → results screen, <b>+50 coins</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
            <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="kfi5nJb7ZB8" data-title="Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 13 Grocery Store walkthrough"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 13 Grocery Store walkthrough">
        <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kfi5nJb7ZB8/maxresdefault.jpg"
             alt="Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 13 Grocery Store walkthrough" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1280" height="720"
             onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kfi5nJb7ZB8/hqdefault.jpg'">
      </div>
    </div>

    <img class="hero" src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-hero-grocery-store.jpg" alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 2 Level 13 Grocery Store: isometric store interior with green walls, a produce island, glass-door drinks fridges, a chest freezer and a blue locker bank" width="1200" height="594" />

    <h2>What this level actually is<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The Grocery Store is one big room, and unlike most rooms in Chapter 2 it is not a puzzle box with a corridor behind it. The camera sits high and looks down into an isometric shop: green walls with a yellow stripe, a pale blue floor, a bakery counter and two packaged-goods aisles down the left wall, two glass-door drinks fridges and a chest freezer along the back wall under a "NEW" poster, a long produce island down the middle — oranges, apples, pears, coconuts, peppers, greens — and a battery of self-checkout tills with three turnstiles at the front. In the back-right corner there is a blue bank of lockers with a yellow-framed screen above it, and beside the lockers a potted plant and a small counter with a bird ornament on it. Everything you need is in that one frame. Nothing is behind a door.</p>
    <p>That is exactly why the level runs long. It is not a room with a hard puzzle in it; it is a room with a dozen live objects and a chain that only closes at the end. The gate is a <b>hand barcode reader</b>, and you get it from a puzzle that does not look like a puzzle — a grid of numbered circles on the locker screen. Until you have the reader you can walk the produce, open the fridges, tap the tins and open the freezer and nothing progresses, because four separate barcodes in this shop have to be read and only the reader can read them.</p>
    <p>The other thing that makes the room feel bigger than it is: it contains <b>two five-slot displays</b> that look identical — same grey plate, same five little windows, same seven-segment digits. One sits under the drinks fridge and takes <b>02725</b>. The other sits under the self-checkout till and ends on <b>65219</b>. Players who find the fridge panel first reasonably assume it is the exit lock, and then spend ten minutes trying to feed it a code they have not earned yet. They are two different machines, two different codes, and one of them is not an input at all.</p>
    <p>Length is the honest measure of the room: our recording clears it in <b>16:02</b> of level time, a second recording manages <b>15:03</b>, and neither of them is fast. There is no timer, no fail state, no way to lock yourself out. The only unrecoverable mistake in the Grocery Store is walking past the wallet.</p>

    <h2>The route at a glance<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <table class="tldr">
      <thead><tr><th>You need</th><th>Where it is</th><th>What it unlocks</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Wallet</td><td>Blue basket by the self-scan tills</td><td>Dismantles into the coin and the 58431267 Code card</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Green shovel</td><td>Blue locker bank, back-right corner</td><td>Digging the flower pot for a gear part</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Hand reader</td><td>Reward for the locker-screen number board</td><td>Every barcode in the shop</td></tr>
        <tr><td>02725</td><td>Five dials under the drinks fridge</td><td>Key to the second drinks fridge, and the bottle</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Two gear parts</td><td>Chest freezer pane + flower pot</td><td>Combined into the juicer's gear</td></tr>
        <tr><td>65219</td><td>Five-slot plate under the self-checkout till</td><td>The big red button and the exit</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>Step by step<span class="accent">.</span></h2>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1 · 0:24</span>
      <strong>Read the room before you touch anything</strong>
      The level opens on a wide shot, which is the only moment the whole shop is visible without a panel over half the screen. Learn four anchors and you will never be lost in this room: the <b>produce island</b> in the middle, the <b>drink fridges and chest freezer</b> along the back wall, the <b>blue lockers</b> with the yellow screen in the back-right corner, and the <b>self-checkout tills</b> with the turnstiles at the front. The thing you are leaving through is at the front of the shop, and it will not open until the last thirty seconds of the level.
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=24s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:24</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2 · 1:04</span>
      <strong>The blue lockers hand you a green shovel</strong>
      Tap the locker bank in the back-right corner. The doors pop open one after another with a small sparkle and one compartment gives you a <b>green shovel</b>. That is the entire contents of the lockers — there is no code on them at this point and no reason to count them. The shovel waits in your bag for a long time: its job is the flower pot beside the lockers, and you cannot do that job until you have a bottle of water later in the level.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-lockers.jpg" alt="The blue locker bank in the Grocery Store with a yellow-framed screen above it and compartments sparking open" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=64s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:04</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3 · 1:29</span>
      <strong>The wallet, and why you dismantle it</strong>
      The blue shopping basket by the self-scan tills holds a brown <b>wallet</b>. Take it, open the bag and press <b>Dismantle</b> — not Use, not Examine. It splits into two items: a <b>Coin</b> and a printed card labelled <b>Code</b> reading <b>58431267</b>. Look at those digits for a second: every number from 1 to 8 appears exactly once. That is not a serial number. It is an ordering of eight things, and there are eight buttons under the vent cover. Our capture opens the bag at 1:29 with the coin, the card and the shovel already in it; those three items are the whole toolkit for the first half of the room.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-basket-wallet.jpg" alt="The blue shopping basket by the Grocery Store self-checkout tills with a brown wallet inside" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-inventory-tools.jpg" alt="The Grocery Store inventory holding a coin, the 58431267 Code card and a green shovel" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=30s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:30</a> · bag at <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=89s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:29</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 · 1:30</span>
      <strong>The coin opens the vent</strong>
      The grey <b>vent cover</b> with four screws is the first lock in the room, and it is not a code lock — it is a screwdriver job. Select the <b>coin</b>, tap each of the four screws, and the cover comes away. Behind it sits a brushed metal plate with <b>eight round buttons</b> along the bottom, <b>eight rectangular modules</b> along the top with a lamp in each, and a tangle of yellow wires between them. If you have not dismantled the wallet, this is where the level stops dead: there is no other use for the coin and no other way in.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-vent-panel.jpg" alt="The grey vent cover with four screws in the Grocery Store" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=90s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:30</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5 · 3:48</span>
      <strong>Eight buttons, eight lamps, one order</strong>
      This is the panel people lose ten minutes on. The eight round buttons at the bottom are wired to the eight lamp modules at the top, and — this is the trap — <b>not to the module directly above them</b>. The wires are drawn as a tangle, so the mapping is not readable by eye and guessing is a waste of time. The correct press order is the one printed on the <b>Code card</b> in your bag: eight positions, numbered 1 to 8. Our capture shows the presses landing one at a time, the round buttons taking a lighter centre as they are used, and the plate releasing at the end of the sequence. It never shows a wrong press, so we cannot tell you what a mistake costs. We do not print a press order here — the card's dot pattern would not resolve twice at our capture resolution, and a wrong order costs more time than opening the bag.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-wire-buttons.jpg" alt="The eight-button vent panel with yellow wires and a row of lamp modules in the Grocery Store" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=228s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3:48</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 6 · 7:29</span>
      <strong>The number board on the locker screen</strong>
      Clearing the buttons opens a second puzzle on the screen above the lockers: a light panel holding a <b>4×6 grid of 24 circles</b>, a handful of them already carrying numbers. You draw one continuous line. The line fills numbers into the circles it crosses, and the numbers already printed on the board have to be reached in the right order as you go — the board is checking a route, not a sum. Our capture's finished board runs from <b>1 to 21</b>. Clear it and the screen spits out the item the rest of the level depends on.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-number-grid.jpg" alt="The locker screen number board in the Grocery Store, a 4x6 grid of circles with numbers and connecting lines" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=449s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">7:29</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 7 · 7:36</span>
      <strong>The hand reader is the real key to this level</strong>
      The reward is a <b>hand barcode reader</b>, and it goes straight into the bag with the label "Bar code reader". Everything from here on is scanning. Four barcodes in this shop have to be read before the till at the front will wake up, and every one of them is on an object you have already walked past. If you are stuck with a full-looking inventory and nothing to do, check that this item is in it.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-barcode-scanner.jpg" alt="The hand barcode reader selected in the Grocery Store inventory" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=456s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">7:36</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 · 8:05</span>
      <strong>Three pickups in the produce island</strong>
      The produce is not scenery and it is not optional. Three taps matter: the <b>orange</b> out of the orange bin, the <b>hammer</b> out of the coconut bin, and the <b>marker</b> out of the pear crate. All three are needed later and none of them can be substituted: the orange goes into the juicer, the hammer is the only thing that breaks the freezer pane, and the marker is what makes one tin's barcode readable. Our capture takes the pears first and comes back for the rest, which is fine — there is no order here, only the obligation to take all three.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-fruit-stands.jpg" alt="A crate of green pears in the Grocery Store produce island" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=485s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">8:05</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 9 · 8:22</span>
      <strong>The tins by the bread, and the soda can</strong>
      Two barcodes live on this shelf. The run of tins next to the bread counter — a blue <b>Baker Oats</b> and a green biscuit tin — carries printed barcodes; the marker goes on the middle tin first, then you read it with the hand reader. In the same pass, open the drinks aisle and read the <b>yellow soda can</b>. Each read is a single tap with the reader selected. You do not have to memorise anything: the reader stores what it reads.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-cans-barcode.jpg" alt="Cans on a Grocery Store shelf with visible barcodes, including Baker Oats and a biscuit tin" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=502s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">8:22</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 10 · 9:30</span>
      <strong>The drinks fridge: five cans, five digits, 02725</strong>
      The glass-door drinks fridge with <b>five square buttons</b> under its shelves is a code machine disguised as a shop fixture. Tap a row of cans and they spin; one can in that row has a digit printed on it. Five rows, five digits, and the five-square panel under the shelves takes them one at a time. Our capture reads the five digits as <b>0 2 7 2 5</b>, and the display under the fridge ends on exactly that: <b>02725</b>. Accepted, the fridge mechanism drops a key.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-soda-fridge.jpg" alt="The open drinks fridge in the Grocery Store with rows of cans and five square buttons under the shelves" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=570s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">9:30</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 11 · 10:02</span>
      <strong>The key, the second fridge, the bottle</strong>
      The key does not open the exit and it does not open the lockers. It opens the <b>second glass-door drinks fridge</b>, and inside there is a single <b>bottle</b> — empty, and the most reused object in the level. It carries water to the flower pot and then sits under the juicer spout. This frame is the dial plate the moment before it accepted 02725; the key drops into the bag with no fanfare and no label prompt.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-fridge-code.jpg" alt="The five-slot dial display under the Grocery Store drinks fridge reading 02725" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=602s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">10:02</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 12 · 11:35</span>
      <strong>The chest freezer: one barcode and one gear part</strong>
      The blue chest freezer at the back holds two things you need and one thing that stops you. Read the <b>chocolate ice cream</b>'s barcode with the hand reader — that is the third barcode. Then look at the <b>cracked pane</b> at the end of the case: tapping it does nothing. Select the <b>hammer</b> and hit it, and the glass gives up a <b>gear part</b>. This is the only place the hammer is used, which is why picking it up in the produce section feels arbitrary until now.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-chest-freezer.jpg" alt="The blue chest freezer in the Grocery Store with three glass compartments" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=694s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">11:35</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 13 · 12:15</span>
      <strong>The flower pot, and the second gear part</strong>
      The pot beside the lockers looks decorative and is not. Two steps, in this order: select the <b>bottle</b> and pour it into the soil, then select the <b>green shovel</b> and dig. The <b>second gear part</b> comes out of the watered soil — the order is the puzzle, so do not dig first and then wonder. Open the bag, put the two gear parts together with <b>Combine</b>, and you are holding the <b>gear</b> the juicer is missing.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-flower-pot.jpg" alt="The potted plant beside the Grocery Store lockers with something buried in the soil" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=734s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">12:15</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 14 · 13:12</span>
      <strong>The juicer: orange, gear, bottle, button</strong>
      The juicer stands by the plant. Four actions and they are strictly ordered: drop the <b>orange</b> into the hopper on top; open the small door under the hopper and seat the <b>gear</b> in the empty socket; set the <b>bottle</b> under the spout; press the <b>button</b>. The machine runs, fills the bottle with juice and prints a <b>receipt</b>. That receipt is the fourth barcode — read it with the hand reader and the scanning half of the level is done.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-juicer.jpg" alt="The Grocery Store juicer with a hopper of oranges and a spout below" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=792s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">13:12</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 15 · 14:27</span>
      <strong>The till by the baskets: the dot grid</strong>
      Back to the self-checkout battery where you found the wallet. Put the <b>hand reader</b> on the till and its screen turns into a <b>grid of dots</b>. This is a state puzzle, not a drawing puzzle: you are not tracing a shape, you are working the grid until every dot is lit the same colour. Tap a dot, watch which dots change with it, and work the board until it is uniform. Our capture takes it slowly and finishes with the whole grid green — and the screen then goes to a single barcode, which is the last thing this shop has to say.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-scanner-puzzle.jpg" alt="The Grocery Store till screen showing a grid of dots after the hand reader is placed" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=867s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">14:27</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 16 · 16:26</span>
      <strong>Dial 65219, then press the red button</strong>
      The last lock is the five-slot plate under the counter by the tills. It starts at <b>00000</b> and each slot is its own dial; the code this end of the level wants is <b>65219</b>. Our capture dials 6-5-2-1-9 with the last slot turning from 8 to 9, and the plate closes the moment it reads <b>65219</b>. Under it is a flat plate with one <b>big red button</b>: press that, the camera pulls back to the wide shop, the front turnstiles release, and the level ends on the results panel — <b>+50 coins</b>, <b>16:02</b>.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-counter-code.jpg" alt="The Grocery Store till display showing 65219 on five seven-segment digits" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l13-level-complete.jpg" alt="The Level Completed screen for Chapter 2 Level 13 with a +50 coin reward and a time of 16:02" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=986s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">16:26</a> · results at <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfi5nJb7ZB8&t=991s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">16:31</a></div>
    </div>
    <h2>The two five-slot panels, and how to tell them apart<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>This is the single most useful thing to understand about the Grocery Store. The level contains two devices that look the same — grey plate, five little windows, seven-segment digits — and they behave completely differently.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>The fridge panel (02725).</b> It sits under the drinks fridge, directly beneath five square buttons. You build this code yourself: five rows of cans, five revealed digits, five dials, starting from 00000. It is an <em>input</em>, and the reward is the key and then the bottle.</li>
      <li><b>The till panel (65219).</b> It sits under the self-checkout counter where you found the wallet, and it also starts at 00000. This one takes the exit code, which is the number the shop gives up at the very end — after the dot grid on the till screen clears and the screen settles on a barcode. Same hardware, different code, and only this one finishes the level: under it is the single red button.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Read that again if you are currently staring at a five-slot display and nothing you do makes it accept anything: the chance that you are at the wrong one of the two is high. If there are five square buttons over the display, you are at the fridge and the code is 02725. If the display sits on a counter with one red button under it, you are at the till and the code is 65219 — and if you have not cleared the dot grid yet, you have not earned the right to be here.</p>

    <h2>Why people get stuck<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>The wallet is in a basket, not a drawer.</b> It is the only item in the room that gates everything else, and it is sitting in plain sight next to the tills. If the vent cover will not come off and you have no coin, you have not tapped the basket.</li>
      <li><b>Dismantle, not Use.</b> The wallet does nothing on its own. The two items that matter only exist after you press the third verb in the inventory bar, and most players never press it in the first half of a level.</li>
      <li><b>The vent buttons are not above their lamps.</b> Everyone's first instinct is to press the eight buttons in the order of the modules over them. The wires are drawn tangled, so the mapping cannot be read by eye. The order is on the card.</li>
      <li><b>The number board looks like decoration.</b> It is a pale grid of circles on a screen; nothing about it says "drag a line". Until you draw, nothing happens, and you can leave the room without the barcode reader and never understand why the tills are inert.</li>
      <li><b>The cans only show their digits while they spin.</b> Tap a row, watch the can that turns, and tap again if you miss it. Reading all five takes a few passes.</li>
      <li><b>The pot will not give up its gear dry.</b> Water first, shovel second. Doing it the other way round is silent failure — no message, no animation, just nothing.</li>
      <li><b>65219 is not the end.</b> It is the last number, but the level finishes on the red button under it. Players who read the code and wait for a door to open stand in front of it for a while.</li>
      <li><b>The exit is at the front.</b> The turnstiles you entered through are the way out; there is no back-room door and no loading bay to find.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="warn">
      <b>What we could not verify:</b> the order the eight vent buttons want, and the exact path the locker board accepts. Both were played correctly on the recording — the lamps fill and the board completes — but the sources of both answers (the dot pattern on the Code card, and the printed numbers on the board) are too small to read twice at our capture resolution, and we are not going to print a sequence we might have wrong. Use the card in your bag for the vent, and work the board's printed numbers in order. The 02725 and 65219 readings are a different case: both were read at 6× zoom with the segment pattern of every digit checked, and 65219 also appears as the terminal value in a second recording.
    </div>

    <h2>Chapter 2 levels<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p class="grid-note">The Grocery Store is the thirteenth room of the twenty-six in Chapter 2, between the Jewelry Store and the Exchange Office. The list below reflects what is written up so far.</p>
    <LevelSelector chapter={2} current={13} compact={true} label="Chapter 2 · No Honor Among Thieves" />

    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is the final code in Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 13?</summary><p><b>65219</b>. It goes into the five-slot plate under the self-checkout counter near the self-scan tills, and that plate starts at 00000. Our recording dials 6-5-2-1-9, reads the last slot turning from 8 to 9, and the plate closes the moment it reads 65219; a second recording of the same level also ends on that number. Under the plate is one big red button, and pressing it finishes the level.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is the code on the drinks fridge dials?</summary><p><b>02725</b>. The fridge with five square buttons under its shelves hides one digit inside each row of cans: tap a row, the cans spin, and one can shows a number. The five digits are 0-2-7-2-5, and the five dials under that fridge start at 00000 and take them one slot at a time. Accepted, the fridge drops a key.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where do I get the coin and the code card?</summary><p>From the wallet in the blue shopping basket by the self-scan tills. Take the wallet, open the inventory, select it and press <b>Dismantle</b>: it splits into a <b>Coin</b> and a printed card labelled <b>Code</b> that reads <b>58431267</b>. The coin is the only tool that opens the vent, and the card is what the eight vent buttons are for.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I get the vent cover off?</summary><p>Select the coin from the inventory and tap each of the four screws on the grey vent cover. The cover comes away and exposes a brushed panel with eight round buttons along the bottom and eight modules with lamps along the top, wired together with yellow tangles. The buttons do not correspond to the modules directly above them, so work from the order the Code card gives, not from the layout.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where is the green shovel?</summary><p>In the blue locker bank in the back-right corner of the store, under the yellow-framed screen. Tap the lockers, let the bank open, and take the green shovel. It is the only item in the lockers, and you need it later on the flower pot beside them.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I fix the juicer and get the receipt?</summary><p>Four things, in this order: drop the orange into the hopper on top, open the small door under the hopper and seat the combined gear in the empty socket, set the bottle under the spout, then press the button. It runs, fills the bottle and prints a receipt. Read the receipt with the hand barcode reader to log the last barcode.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where are the two gear parts?</summary><p>One is inside the chest freezer at the back, behind the cracked pane that only the hammer will break. The other is buried in the flower pot beside the lockers: pour the bottle into the soil first, then dig with the green shovel. Combine the two parts in the inventory and you get the gear the juicer is missing.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How long does the Grocery Store take and what does it pay?</summary><p>The recording finishes it in <b>16:02</b> of level time for <b>+50 coins</b>; a second, faster recording clears the same room in <b>15:03</b>. There is no timer and no fail state. The length comes from four barcodes and two five-digit panels, not from difficulty.</p></details>

